        <div class="faq-item">
          <button type="button" class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">
            <span class="faq-q-text">Is the serum safe for Indian skin specifically?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon"></span>
          </button>

          <div class="faq-a">
            <div class="faq-a-inner">
              <p>Yes. Fitzpatrick IV-VI skin (which covers most Indian skin tones) is more susceptible to PIH, post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation, from harsh actives. Our formulations avoid the ingredients most likely to cause PIH while directly targeting melanin transfer through the Kojic Acid and Niacinamide systems in the Dark Spots serum.</p><p>The bio-retinoids are specifically chosen because they don't trigger the inflammatory response that causes PIH in higher-melanin skin.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
    
  
    
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button type="button" class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">
            <span class="faq-q-text">I'm 24. Am I too young to start?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon"></span>
          </button>

          <div class="faq-a">
            <div class="faq-a-inner">
              <p>24 is one of the best times to start. Skin longevity isn't about reversing damage later. It's about protecting and building structure while you still have it. The earlier you support collagen, barrier, and hydration, the longer they hold.</p><p>This isn't an anti-ageing product you graduate into at 40. It's a maintenance protocol for skin you want to keep.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
